    19	> strictly worse than the existing O(x^{1/2+ε}) zero-summation barrier.
    20	
    21	Thread 2's adversarial challenge: **does this argument survive
    22	amortisation?** Specifically, the operator's spectrum is *universal*
    23	(zeta zeros do not depend on x). One could in principle diagonalise
    24	once, cache K eigenvalues, and serve many π(x) queries via the
    25	explicit-formula partial sum at per-query cost O(K).
    26	
    27	If amortisation collapses argument 2, only S53's argument 1 (rank-one
    28	parameter count) and argument 3 (CCM's geometric error growth) remain.
